// Druidic Ritual gate for Herblore (Corey, 2026-09-05).
//
// A note on authenticity, because this is a deliberate departure. In 2006 there was no explicit
// quest check on Herblore actions - identify.rs2 still carries the comment "early osrs had no
// druidic ritual check. This is how level 2 herblore accounts were possible". The block was
// implicit and worked by arithmetic: you start at Herblore 1, the cheapest action (cleaning a guam)
// needs 3, and Druidic Ritual grants exactly 250 xp, which is level 3. The one way to reach level 3
// without the quest was an xp lamp, and lamps ARE quest-gated (see general/scripts/xplamp).
//
// Corey chose the explicit check, which is how modern OSRS does it: clearer to the player, and it
// closes the hole if any future xp source lands Herblore levels some other way.

[proc,herblore_requires_druidic_ritual]()(boolean)
if (%druidquest < ^druid_complete) {
    mes("You need to complete the Druidic Ritual quest before you can use the Herblore skill.");
    return(false);
}
return(true);
